cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Code is MIT; the paper text and figures are CC BY 4.0. If you use this work, cite the repository and the working paper."
type: software
title: "Epistemic-Aware DRO for Mean-CVaR Portfolios"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered research apparatus for testing whether ML epistemic
  uncertainty improves the tail-risk/return trade-off of a distributionally
  robust mean-CVaR ETF portfolio. v1 completed with H1/H3 failing and H2
  passing; v2 and v3 were stopped before the holdout when their information
  gates failed. The 2025-2026 holdout remains untouched. No alpha claim, no
  live deployment, and no investment advice.
authors:
  - family-names: Talingting
    given-names: Ken Ira Lacson
